# Status Overlook workspace

This repo **implements** Status Overlook (CLI + digests + optional localhost UI). Before non-trivial changes, read [docs/AGENT_CONTEXT.md](../../docs/AGENT_CONTEXT.md) for full handoff detail.

## Agent data contract

Digests on disk (`digest.md` / `digest.json`) or `status-overlook show --plain` — **not** the browser UI for automation.

## Pipeline

`init` → `reconcile` (discover via `acli`/`gh`) → `enrich` + `classify` → `store` → `digest` → `show` / `serve`

`status-overlook run` = reconcile (unless skipped) → enrich/classify → save store → write digests.

| Stage | Module |
|-------|--------|
| Discover | `providers/jira.py`, `providers/github.py` |
| Merge | `store.reconcile` |
| Enrich | `enrich.py` |
| Classify | `classify_jira.py`, `classify_github.py`, `classify_github_issue.py` (pure, no I/O) |
| Present | `digest.py`, `term_show.py`, `serve.py` |

## Three sources (IDs must not collide)

| Source | `source` | Store id prefix | Discovery |
|--------|----------|-----------------|-----------|
| Jira | `jira` | `jira:KEY` | `acli` assigned + QA-in-Testing |
| GitHub PR | `github_pr` | `github-pr:owner/repo#n` | `gh search prs` author **or** assignee |
| GitHub Issue | `github_issue` | `github-issue:owner/repo#n` | `gh search issues --assignee=@me` **only** |

Legacy: `source=github` / `github:…` for PRs migrates on load via `store.normalize_*`.

`pins.github` → PRs; `pins.github_issues` → issues. `skip_github` skips **both**.

## Timestamps (do not conflate)

- `state_changed_at` — last successfully observed visible-state change (lifecycle, action, remote status, or displayed cue). No-op runs and reason-only changes must **not** bump it; rendered age is derived from this timestamp.
- `last_read_at` — user/agent mark-read; unread when `state_changed_at` is after this.

## Action states

`actionable` | `pending` | `blocked` | `done` | `ignore`

Section order: **Actionable → Pending → Blocked → Recently done**.

Classification rules: [docs/DECISIONS.md](../../docs/DECISIONS.md) — do not invent new action states without updating tests and DECISIONS.

Cues (`cues.py`) are display-only next-step labels derived from `reasons` — not new action states and not stored.

Notable: PR authors stay actionable while **any** GraphQL review thread is unresolved (`enrich.probe_pr_review_threads`), not only `CHANGES_REQUESTED`.

## Grouping

Active items collapse in `digest.build_work_groups` (Jira pr_link, PR linked issues, Jira key in title). Recently done is **not** grouped.

## Deferred (do not build without explicit ask)

Team multi-user / ROSA UI, `ghd` provider, write-back to Jira/GitHub, UI polling when only the OS scheduler updates disk.

## Dev workflow

```bash
.venv/bin/pytest tests/ -q          # after behavior changes; no network in default pytest
.venv/bin/status-overlook doctor
.venv/bin/status-overlook run
.venv/bin/status-overlook show --plain
.venv/bin/status-overlook serve --open   # restart serve after Python/static changes
```

Style: stdlib-first; PyYAML for config only; `http.server` for UI. Minimize scope; match neighboring modules.

## Common pitfalls

| Symptom | Likely cause |
|---------|----------------|
| Issue missing from digest | Not assignee-discovered; run full `run`; check `track_store.json` |
| QA Testing ticket missing | Empty `jira.qa_contact_field`; acli search rejects `customfield_*` — enrich uses `workitem view` |
| UI missing view/section | Stale `serve` process — restart |
| UI Refresh: field customfield_* not allowed | Serve loaded enrich before the view-based QA fetch; restart serve (Refresh now reloads enrich.py) |
| Jira items done after `run --skip-jira` | Reconcile finishes absent candidates — use full `run` |
| Grouped row wrong primary | Open PR wins tie-break in `build_work_groups` |
